d 'NEWCOMBE11': module to compute eleven confidence intervals for the difference between two independent binomial proportions
d
d      newcombe11 calculates confidence intervals for the risk
d difference, p1 - p2, between two independent binomial
d proportions,	  using the eleven methods numbered in Newcombe
d (1998). The default is method 10, the combination of uncorrected
d Wilson score	  intervals, with 95% confidence.    In immediate
d syntax, group 1 is x1/n1.  In dataset syntax, group 1 is the
d smaller observed numeric value of group; group 2 is	 the larger
d value.  Observations with missing outcome or group are excluded. 
d Changing group coding can reverse the sign of the    difference. 
d The output explicitly identifies the numeric code of each group
d and displays its value label, if defined. The    difference
d always subtracts the larger-coded group's proportion from the
d smaller-coded group's proportion. Labels do not    change this
d order.  In immediate syntax, the two groups follow the supplied
d argument order. 
d
d KW: risk difference
d KW: confidence intervals
d
d Requires: Stata version 10
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261031
d
d Author: Silvano Andorno , University of Eastern Piedmont "Amedeo Avogadro"  
d Support: email silvano.andorno@@uniupo.it
d
f newcombe11.ado
f newcombe11.sthlp
